From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 07:52:37 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] AP MLD: Free a link station of a removed link without a disconnection

When LINK_REMOVE takes a link out of the AP MLD,
hostapd_free_link_stas() frees the link stations of the non-AP MLDs that
are associated over another link. ap_free_sta() then reports
AP-STA-DISCONNECTED with the MLD address, although the non-AP MLD stays
associated over its other links.

Clear the authorized flag of such a link station without the event
before hostapd frees it, and report CTRL-EVENT-LINK-STA-REMOVED on the
removed link instead. AP-STA-DISCONNECTED stays the event for a
departure of the station. The addition and the deletion of a single
link are reported with CTRL-EVENT-LINK-STA-ADDED and
CTRL-EVENT-LINK-STA-REMOVED, as Link Reconfiguration already does. A
Link Reconfiguration addition also sets the authorized flag of the new
link station without AP-STA-CONNECTED.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---

--- a/src/ap/sta_info.c
+++ b/src/ap/sta_info.c
@@ -634,6 +634,11 @@ void hostapd_free_link_stas(struct hosta
 
 		wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG, "Removing link station from MLD " MACSTR,
 			   MAC2STR(prev->addr));
+		ap_sta_link_event(hapd, WPA_EVENT_LINK_STA_REMOVED, prev->addr,
+				  hapd->mld_link_id);
+		/* The non-AP MLD stays associated over its other links, so no
+		 * disconnection is reported for it. */
+		ap_sta_set_authorized_flag(hapd, prev, 0);
 		ap_free_sta(hapd, prev);
 	}
 }
@@ -2093,6 +2098,14 @@ int ap_sta_pending_delayed_1x_auth_fail_
 
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211BE
+void ap_sta_link_event(struct hostapd_data *hapd, const char *event,
+		       const u8 *addr, u8 link_id)
+{
+	wpa_msg(hapd->msg_ctx, MSG_INFO, "%ssta=" MACSTR " link_id=%u",
+		event, MAC2STR(addr), link_id);
+}
+
+
 static void ap_sta_remove_link_sta(struct hostapd_data *hapd,
 				   struct sta_info *sta)
 {
--- a/src/ap/sta_info.h
+++ b/src/ap/sta_info.h
@@ -489,6 +489,8 @@ void ap_sta_restore_wpa_sm(struct hostap
 			   struct wpa_state_machine *prev_sm);
 int ap_sta_reset_prev_assoc(struct hostapd_data *hapd, struct sta_info *sta,
 			    struct wpa_state_machine *prev_sm);
+void ap_sta_link_event(struct hostapd_data *hapd, const char *event,
+		       const u8 *addr, u8 link_id);
 
 static inline bool ap_sta_is_epp(const struct sta_info *sta)
 {
